l factors contribute to the roughhousing you see. But effective coaching means understanding that biology operates within a social environment that you can design. Separate, stricter supervision for boys risks creating a poor environment that makes those biological tendencies worse, not better. An even expectation with smarter, individualized attention uses the biology to your advantage—and teaches every kid, regardless of gender, that they're capable of controlling their body.
